    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.11_base_commutative_diagram.chapters.25_six_step_bridge_deep_dives.sections.01_mereology_six_step.concrete_anchor_7#mereologicalcongruence_simp" .
silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_25_six_step_bridge_deep_dives_sections_01_mereology_six_step_concrete_anchor_7#mereologicalcongruence_simp silm:hasLongDescription "The MereologicalCongruence_simP is the congruence sim_P generated by all part-identification relators; the equivalence used in the quotient. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'MereologicalCongruence_simP', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
